games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/51"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "400 metres Hurdles, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "5 –  9 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2157"} "Stade de France, Saint-Denis, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2013606"} "39 from 25 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The men’s 400 metre hurdles was highly anticipated, matching two of the greatest intermediate hurdlers ever in defending gold medalist and world record holder " [:a {:href "/athletes/135340"} "Karsten Warholm"] " (NOR) and the United States’ " [:a {:href "/athletes/147346"} "Rai Benjamin"] ". In addition, Brazil’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/141191"} "Alison dos Santos"] " could not be overlooked, as the 2020 bronze medalist, behind Warholm and Benjamin, the 2022 World Champion, and the 2023 Diamond League Champion. Since the Tokyo final, the threesome had met four times, with Benjamin winning twice and Warholm and dos Santos once each."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Warholm won the first semi-final, as dos Santos finished third and had to advance to the final as a time qualifier. Benjamin won the third semi, jogging home in 47.85, while semi two went to " [:a {:href "/athletes/2103714"} "Kyron McMaster"] " of the British Virgin Islands."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Warholm started the final the quickest, as he always does, leading at the fifth hurdle in 20.18, with Benjamin in third and dos Santos fourth. Around the final bend, Benjamin moved ahead, leading by 0.2 at hurdle nine and 0.5 at hurdle 10, as the gold was not in doubt on the final straight. Benjamin crossed in 46.46, the fifth fastest time ever. Warholm was well back in 47.06 for silver, as dos Santos repeated his bronze medal in 47.26."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:t